+### 0. Daemon workflow cutover check (RIG-89)
+
+The daemon can run the ticket factory as a workflow. Both producers must never admit the same
+ticket, so check the daemon before anything else.
+
+```bash
+curl -sf "${RIG_DAEMON_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:7433}/api/ticket-factory/cutover" || echo "daemon-unavailable"
+```
+
+| Result | Action |
+|--------|--------|
+| `daemon-unavailable`, 503, or no `phase` field | Fall back: continue as before. Print "daemon workflow not available; running skill-based factory-loop". |
+| `phase` is `legacy`, `reconciled`, or `rolled-back` | Continue. This skill owns admission. Tickets in `daemonAdmitted` are still skipped (see claim fence). |
+| `phase` is `daemon` | WARN: "daemon workflow owns admission. This skill must not admit new tickets." Stop admitting. Only finish tickets that are already in flight here (restart reconciliation below). |
+
+**Claim fence.** Before claiming any ticket (Step 1 and `--ticket`), skip every ticket id listed in
+the endpoint's `daemonAdmitted` array and print why. If the endpoint is unreachable, claim as before.
+
+**Rollback.** If the daemon workflow fails: run `POST /api/ticket-factory/cutover/rollback`
+(drains the daemon; its active tickets keep running and stay listed in `daemonAdmitted`), confirm
+`phase` is `rolled-back`, then run this skill as usual. See `docs/reference/factory-loop-cutover.md`.
 
